Amount paid for the first half of the year = monthly charge * 6
Amount paid for the first half of the year = $140 * 6
Amount paid for the first half of the year = $840
Then, calculate the 10% less charge for the other half of the year.
10% less of $140 = 10/100 * $140
10% less of $140 = 0.1 * $140
10% less of $140 = $14
So, the reduced monthly charge for the other half of the year is $140 - $14 = $126.
Now, calculate the total amount she paid for the other half of the year.
