2. She writes half of it once: Half of the alphabet is 26 / 2 = 13 letters. Adding this to her total, she now has 52 + 13 = 65 letters.
3. Then, she re-writes everything she has already written: This means we need to add the total letters she has written so far (65) to her new total. Therefore, 65 + 65 = 130 letters.

